  "notes": "うとうと describes light, drowsy sleep — dozing off unintentionally, hovering between wakefulness and sleep.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- うとうとする: to doze off, to nod off\n- うとうとしていた: was dozing\n- {電車|でんしゃ}でうとうとする: to doze on the train\n- うとうとし{始|はじ}める: to start nodding off\n\nUSAGE:\nImplies the sleep is unintentional and light — the person can be easily woken. Often happens in situations like riding a train, sitting in a warm room, or during a boring lecture.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- すやすや: sleeping peacefully, soundly (deeper, more restful)\n- ぐっすり: sleeping deeply, fast asleep\n- {居眠|いねむ}り: dozing (especially at work or school)\n- こっくりこっくり: nodding off (head bobbing motion)",
